xnu 0454: dump the bhi descriptors before and after the doorbell

Measured 2026-11-26: the host side of the MHI/BHI load matches ath11k
register for register (0449-0451), the SMMU records no fault, and the
doorbell is still not consumed. The K60 research in this repository
(research/unixnu-mondrian/docs/research/wifi/SBL-DIRECT.md) shows the same
device does consume the image with the stock host, so the missing piece is
still on this side.

The BHI block carries values the boot ROM writes: BHI_SBLANTIROLLVER and
BHI_NUMSEG. Read them before the SOC reset, after it, and at 1, 10 and 100 ms
after the doorbell, together with the doorbell register itself. A consumed
session id does not stay in BHI_IMGTXDB, and a zero anti-rollback version
after the reset says the drawing board: the PBL never started, so the gate is
the device's power/clock, not the transfer.

Instrumentation only: no register the load path writes changes.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
index 8abc031..28d367d 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_wifi.c
@@ -1263,6 +1263,34 @@ wifi_soc_reset(void)
 	return 0;
